=== 3. measured per-operation cost (cycles @ 250 MHz aclk) ===
From the micro-benchmarks, at three modelled fabric latencies.  LAT is the
one-way latency seq_fabric_model adds on EACH of AW/W, B, AR, R, so it
stands in for the real SmartConnect + axi_register_slice chain.

  micro (records / AXI-Lite ops)      LAT=0    LAT=4    LAT=8   derived cost
  csrwr  2000 writes                   6124     6124     6124   3.06 cyc/write
  cmd    200 cmds (3 CSRWR + CMD)      6550     8899    11125   32.5 cyc/cmd
                                                                overhead at
                                                                LAT=4 (the
                                                                stub's ~12 cyc
                                                                of layer busy
                                                                subtracted)
  ldc    4096 words                   12394    12403    12409   3.03 cyc/word
  movx   4096 words (+ the LDC above) 20620    20668    20716   2.02 cyc/word
  movy16 2048 rows                     6490     6577     6664   3.00 cyc/row
  movy32 2048 rows                    12634    12721    12808   6.00 cyc/row

The mover paths are FLAT in LAT (<0.5% from 0 to 8) because both AXI-Lite
channels are pipelined: MOVY reads matvec RES on one slave while it writes
the dequantized words into the layer scratchpad on another.  Only the CMD
retire path is latency-sensitive, because a CMD must DRAIN its write before
the STATUS poll can mean anything (AXI gives no read/write ordering).

Record fetch is never the limiter: at the maximum sustained issue rate
(csrwr micro, 3.06 cyc/record) with a 32-cycle DDR first-word latency the
prefetch FIFO ran dry for 50 of 6124 cycles (0.8%).

XRF mirror refresh, measured as the delta between the default (AXI-Lite
read-back through layer_chan's XRFI/XRFD window) and USE_XRF_SIDEBAND=1:
  core stream, 4 seeds: 4246/4528/4390/5146  vs  4129/4399/4273/5005 cycles
  -> ~20 cycles per DYNQ16 / op-8-probe refresh, ~8 per DYNQ8 (EOUT is a
     single read).  At 385 refreshes/token that is 6.5k cycles = 0.026 ms,
     0.15% of the sequencer's fabric time.  DECISION: keep the AXI-Lite
     mirror; the sideband port stays implemented but unused (tied off in
     create_project.tcl) because it would need new top-level wiring for
     0.15% of the time.

