  The rung-1 target in docs/SPEEDUP_LADDER.md is 12.2 tok/s = pure 4-chan
  device time.  The sequencer adds 21% on top of it.  IN REACH; the three
  cheap CSR additions below take it to ~10.9 tok/s (91.6 ms/token).

=== 5. where the remaining 17.4 ms goes, and the cheapest ways to cut it ===
88% of it is MOVX+MOVY+LDC, i.e. one AXI-Lite transaction per 16-bit
scratch word, because that is the only path into layer_chan's scratchpad.
Three additions, each a handful of LUTs in a SHIPPED slave, remove 1.89M
cycles/token (7.5 ms), i.e. 10.1 -> 10.9 tok/s:

  a) layer_chan SWIN32: a second scratch-write window taking TWO 16-bit
     words per 32-bit AXI-Lite write.  Halves the MOVY pairs32 write
     stream (the single biggest term, 2.52M cyc) and LDC/EMB.  ~1.37M cyc.
  b) layer_chan packed SWIN read: 4 int8 (or 2 int16) per read.  MOVX
     drops from 277k reads to 69k.  ~0.33M cyc.
  c) matvec_chan RES prefetch (2-deep; see the C1 note in seq_movers.sv):
     removes the 3-cycle RES_DATA pacing MOVY must use today.  ~0.18M cyc.

=== 6. no-wait MVGO (the 4-chan enabler), implemented, ISA-compatible ===
ISA v1.2/v1.3 MVGO is "start, WAIT done", so four channels serialise and
the device term is the 1-chan 112.5 ms, not the 4-chan 81.7 ms.  seq_movers
implements a no-wait variant selected by MVGO target[0] — a field the
validator does not constrain and every emitted stream leaves at 0, so
existing streams are bit-identical: target[0]=1 starts the engine and
returns, and FENCE drains every channel a no-wait MVGO left running.
Exploiting it needs a generator change (agent B) and an ISA note.

=== 7. hardware hazards found by reading the SHIPPED slaves ===
Both are worked around in seq_movers with no change to shipped RTL, and
both are MODELLED in the stubs, so the workaround is verified, not assumed:
  C1 matvec_chan RES_DATA returns a READ_LATENCY_B=2 BRAM output addressed
     by res_ptr and increments res_ptr in the same cycle: two RES_DATA
     reads accepted <3 cycles apart return STALE data.  The host never hit
     it (MMIO reads are ~1.7 us apart).  MOVY paces reads RES_GAP=3.
  C2 matvec_chan STATUS.done is STICKY UNTIL THE NEXT START and the start
     doorbell crosses to ui_clk through a toggle+2FF, so polling done right
     after the doorbell can observe the PREVIOUS run's done.  MVGO waits
     MVGO_GUARD=64 aclk cycles before its first poll (0.1 ms/token total).
